- Story & Context: In the freezing winter of 1997 at Berlin's Lichtspiel Cinema, operator Kaelen Voss patched a deathrock pedal directly into a sub-bass generator while watching atmospheric optical halos form through the booth's iced-over window. The resulting surge of low-end drone vibrated the auditorium floor so violently it shattered a glass framed portrait of F.W. Murnau, cementing the genre's birthed sound. Sallow improvised her first vocal loop over the trembling floor, weeping real tears into the ribbon mic as the silver halide film melted in the gate. "In the bright refraction of the halo light, we burn the film to keep the cinema warm."
